  },
  {
    "insert": "\n\nThe document underscores the importance of the issue by highlighting the communication gap between healthcare providers and patients during the perioperative phase. It points out that poor communication may lead to misunderstandings and adverse patient outcomes. While the significance is apparent, the argument could be strengthened by including specific examples or data to demonstrate the extent and effects of this issue. For instance, statistics regarding patient dissatisfaction or complications post-surgery linked to communication failures would make the problem more tangible. \n\n"
